From: liuqin Fedora adaptation <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] liuqin 7.3.1: camcc-sm8450: park the camera RCGs when disabled

Upstream commit 704930b1a253 ("clk: qcom: camcc-sm8450: Park the camera RCGs
when they are disabled"), applied 2026-11-08, i.e. after the 7.3.1 baseline.

The camera RCGs use clk_rcg2_ops, so a disabled RCG stays configured on
whichever PLL it last ran from.  Once that PLL is turned off and Titan top
collapses after a camera session, the next session's CSID reset never
completes (observed here as "CSID reset timeout" / -EIO on the second
capture).  clk_rcg2_shared_ops parks the RCG on XO while disabled and
reconfigures it on enable.  cam_cc_sleep_clk_src runs from the always-on
sleep clock and is left alone.

The companion commit c1793791923d ("Retain flops across camera GDSC
collapse") is already covered by the local camcc GDSC changes in 0006.
The eUSB clkref part of the same series (0645645582ee) is unrelated and not
included.

Original-Author: Sushmit Singh Rathore <sushmit718@gmail.com>
Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/704930b1a25310c1357e9f7f9b6d0f4aff95a459
Linux-derived code retains original GPL notices. Offline port; no hardware claim.
